.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-BENCHMARK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-benchmark
.Nd compare native Metal and Rosetta inference speed
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad benchmark
.Op Cm run
.Op Ar model
.Nm nomad benchmark
.Cm patch-host
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the same model and prompt twice on this Mac: once on the native Ollama
daemon using Metal, and once in a forced
.Cm linux/amd64
container under Rosetta.
It reports the eval rate
.Pq tokens per second
and total wall time for each path, and prints a Markdown table suitable for a
README.
.Pp
With no subcommand,
.Nm
runs
.Cm run .
The optional model argument defaults to
.Cm llama3.1:8b .
The model is pulled into each path if not already present.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm run Op Ar model
Run the native-versus-Rosetta comparison.
This is the default.
.It Cm patch-host
Patch the latest benchmark row recorded by the admin service with this Mac's
real host hardware
.Pq the Apple chip and Metal GPU .
Containers cannot see Metal, so admin records empty CPU and GPU fields that
otherwise submit as a dash to the upstream leaderboard; this fills them in
before the row is submitted from the UI.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad benchmark
Run the comparison with the default model.
.It Ic nomad benchmark run qwen2.5-coder:7b
Run the comparison with a specific model.
.It Ic nomad benchmark patch-host
Inject this Mac's real hardware into the admin leaderboard row.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-models 1
